description:
Repo: imkarrer/workstation. New file: darwin/ai.nix, imported from flake.nix modules list.

The cask runs Ollama as a macOS app, which never reads .zshrc, so exported shell variables are silently ignored. The common workaround is running `launchctl setenv` by hand, which is exactly the undeclared state this repo exists to eliminate. Use nix-darwin's declarative equivalent:

  launchd.user.envVariables = {
    OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE      = "30m";    # 30m on the laptop; -1 on the Mac Studio
    OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH  = "16384";  # default is 2048 and will ruin RAG
    OLLAMA_FLASH_ATTENTION = "1";
    OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL    = "4";      # retune from load-test results
  };

Keep this out of the captured-defaults machinery (darwin/defaults.generated.nix is written by capture-defaults.sh; do not hand-edit it).
